    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0413" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AA/6–1146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Acting United States Representative at the United Nations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-19T19:00:00-04:00">June 19, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. Amdel. Urtel 302, June 11, 3 p.m. 1. Re your paragraph one and your
                    suggestion on chairmanship membership committee in your para two, we feel
                    questions should be settled locally in accordance with views and convenience of
                    all members and not as major issues. In addition to your suggestion and that of
                    rotation with presidency, you may wish consider following: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Beginning rotation at head of alphabet, with Australia, as Atomic
                            Energy Commission has done;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Electing one chairman for whole busy period of committee.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0414" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/>
                <p>We particularly suggest alternative (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) as
                    application of rotation principle that avoids further concentration of work on
                    delegation of Council president. If Council continues to create standing
                    committees it may become impracticable to rotate chairmanship of all
                    simultaneously.</p>
                <p>Shortness of committee’s main period of work seems to make (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) worth consideration also.</p>
                <p>2. Your course stated in para 3 is approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
